    "keys": [
      "10.18419/darus-3152",
      "Validation data for comparison of SMC-PI controllers vs. P-PI controller"
    ],
    "matched_files": [],
    "scope": "1141 tracked evidence paths including gzip bodies, 301 further archived members, early baseline-index; Unicode-normalized DOI and title."
  },
  "apparatus": "Shared Stuttgart 400 kg ball-screw / linear direct-drive table, 0.72 m travel. The README explicitly refers to the magnetic force compensation from 10.18419/darus-2563. In the author thesis, Appendix A.3 identifies Heidenhain LS187C table linear scale, separate AM2048S/R motor encoder and four Kistler 9323A sensors. Treat as repeated studies on one rig.",
  "shared_bench_identity": "File bytes SHA-256 plus complete native x_meas_table array serialized as contiguous little-endian float64, one digest per MATLAB acquisition. All six pairwise comparisons among darus-2563/3109/3003/3152 have zero exact content matches on both tests. Partial subsequences, rerendered runs and related settings are outside this equality test.",
  "methods": [
    "Used channel-specific MATLAB dSPACE XIndex and nearest timestamps on the first nominal 1 kHz grid; rejected any row with a required or present optional channel farther than 0.1251 ms. Retained points coincide exactly with source timestamps. Inverter torque comes from the drive; table position is a separate encoder signal.",
    "Computed whole-file error and error restricted to planned absolute speed >0.01 m/s. From 10 DStep files extracted onset steps with |force increment| >500 N and preceding absolute force below 250 N, to allow for compensation baseline. Per step, subtracted preceding 100 ms median table error, then computed peak absolute change in the first 100 ms."
  ],
  "results": [
    "110 physical records cover 747,561 synchronized position, inverter and command rows with no unpaired rows. The 19 PT2I-selection files carry enable and error flags. None of the 110 release F_nut_sum. Four MillingSim records apply simulated disturbance waveforms to physical moving equipment.",
    "20 opposite-sign approximately 1 kN step onsets were verified. First-100-ms peak table error spans 123.35–155.01 µm across the P-PI control files, 35.62–67.77 µm across linear sliding-mode gains, and 27.97–59.79 µm across quasi-sliding-mode gains. The two K=400 quasi-SMC peaks are 27.97 and 32.94 µm.",
    "Protocol.md identifies the gain-400 qSMC disturbance sweep as unstable, and the archive has no corresponding MAT file; no_DSweep.txt records high excitation. The protocol also says qSMC with +210 kg needs retuning; neither velocity profile is supplied for this setting. qSMC +105 kg files are present."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The disturbance signal is the commanded force, not independent contact or cutting-force measurement. Measurements at fixed gain are repeated trial conditions; a good step result does not establish broadband stability. The omitted sweep is documented selection, with no associated failure trace.",
    "The 19 PT2I-selection records evaluate inverse-model feedforward with feedback off according to Experiments.md. The 91 remaining numeric files omit enable/error channels; missing flags cannot be interpreted as normal control."
  ],
